github.com/users/tsegismont/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-19T10:00:06Z","updated_at":"2021-05-19T10:00:06Z","body":"@FroMage in Vert.x Web applications, if you want to upgrade to websocket connection in a route handler you must make sure:\r\n\r\n- no previous route invokes `routingContext.next()` asynchronously, or\r\n- the request is paused immediately when received and not resumed before upgrading\r\n\r\nI discussed this briefly with @phillip-kruger and he told me there are other route handlers than his and when he gets the request notification it is too late, the request has already been read.\r\n\r\nDo you have any idea which route handlers that could be?\r\n\r\nAlso, I'm wondering what that means for Quarkus Reactive Routes. Would users always be notified in their route handlers when the request has already been read?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/843947054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"tsegismont","id":1500598,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDA1OTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1500598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont","html_url":"https://github.com/tsegismont","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegismont/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsegi